      10["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Web UI</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Python, Streamlit, OIDC login]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Browser interface for<br />uploading exports, launching<br />and monitoring runs,<br />exploring results with<br />evidence highlighted in the<br />note, reviewing errors,<br />reviewing and adjudicating<br />rows, blind labelling and<br />reading KPIs. Holds no<br />business logic: it calls the<br />Run Console, Human Review<br />System and stores.</div>"]
      style 10 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#343ced,color:#272834
      101["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Synthetic Data Generator</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Python, Faker, local LLM (optional)]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Generates synthetic dispute<br />exports with gold items by<br />construction, for the public<br />repo, demos, poster, unit<br />tests and adversarial<br />guardrail tests; checks<br />fidelity, privacy and<br />validity before a synthetic<br />set is published.</div>"]
      style 101 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#343ced,color:#272834
      107["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Configuration Registry</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: YAML in Git, JSON Schema, pydantic]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>The configurable layer. Typed<br />parameters with limits,<br />owner, change log and<br />validity horizon; layered<br />resolution core -><br />environment -> carrier<br />override; every resolved<br />config is hashed into the run<br />manifest.</div>"]
      style 107 fill:#d8f1f6,stroke:#ef601b,color:#272834
      111[("<div style='font-weight: bold'>Version & Artifact Registry</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Filesystem CAS + DuckDB, Git tags]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Content-addressed store and<br />lineage index for every<br />versioned artifact: input<br />snapshots, taxonomy,<br />evaluation sets, prompts,<br />lexicon, calibration maps,<br />model identities, run<br />manifests, outputs, KPI<br />snapshots.</div>")]
      style 111 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#ef601b,color:#272834
      112[("<div style='font-weight: bold'>Ground Truth Store</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Parquet + DuckDB, access-controlled folder]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Approved charge taxonomy<br />(D1), sealed locked test set<br />(D2), DEV set, FRESH set and<br />labelling records. Test<br />labels are readable only by<br />the KPI Calculator.</div>")]
      style 112 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#343ced,color:#272834
      113[("<div style='font-weight: bold'>Telemetry & Episode Store</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: DuckDB]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Action telemetry (what<br />happened), decision telemetry<br />(why) and outcome telemetry<br />(what followed), linked by<br />case_id and tagged with the<br />run's version.</div>")]
      style 113 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#343ced,color:#272834
      22["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Run Console</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Python 3.12, Typer CLI]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Command-line entry point and<br />the only pipeline<br />orchestrator: 'itemizer run<br /><export.xlsx>'. Resolves<br />configuration, opens a run<br />manifest, runs the stages,<br />and exposes evaluate / review<br />/ promote sub-commands. The<br />Web UI launches runs through<br />it.</div>"]
      style 22 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#ef601b,color:#272834
      26["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Data Transformation & Check</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Python, pandas, openpyxl]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Reads the TMS Excel export,<br />validates it against the<br />input contract, normalizes<br />fields, fingerprints and<br />de-duplicates notes, masks<br />names, and writes an<br />immutable input snapshot.</div>"]
      style 26 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#343ced,color:#272834
      33["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Model Router</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Python]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Decides which model handles<br />each note, enforces the<br />confidentiality gate, applies<br />fallback, caches responses by<br />content hash and meters<br />tokens and cost. The provider<br />interface is the exit path.</div>"]
      style 33 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#ef601b,color:#272834
      42["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Local Model Runtime</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Ollama]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Self-hosted open-weights<br />model used when external AI<br />is not approved, and as the<br />tested fallback.</div>"]
      style 42 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#8b8c9c,color:#272834
      43["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Itemization Classifier</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Python, pydantic]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Turns one note into charge<br />items with category, amount<br />and exact evidence span using<br />a bounded tool-calling LLM<br />agent; checks evidence,<br />reconciles to the disputed<br />amount, scores confidence and<br />assigns the row outcome.<br />Never invents or edits an<br />amount.</div>"]
      style 43 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#343ced,color:#272834
      53["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Output Formatter</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Python, openpyxl]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Writes the Excel deliverable:<br />items sheet (one line per<br />charge with evidence), row<br />summary sheet (outcome,<br />totals, discrepancy) and a<br />run info sheet carrying the<br />manifest.</div>"]
      style 53 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#343ced,color:#272834
      54["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Human Review System</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Python, openpyxl]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Review service behind the Web<br />UI: builds the review queue<br />within reviewer capacity,<br />validates and records<br />approvals, edits and<br />adjudications, runs blind<br />labelling for the test set,<br />and closes cases. An Excel<br />review workbook remains as an<br />offline fallback.</div>"]
      style 54 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#343ced,color:#272834
      61["<div style='font-weight: bold'>KPI Calculator</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Python, pandas, scikit-learn, SciPy]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Computes every success and<br />error metric from immutable,<br />versioned inputs only, per<br />population (TEST, DEV, FRESH,<br />PROD), with sample sizes,<br />weights and confidence<br />intervals, and evaluates the<br />Level 1/2/3 gates.</div>"]
      style 61 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#343ced,color:#272834
      74["<div style='font-weight: bold'>KPI Dashboard</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Python, Jinja2, Vega-Lite]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Static, self-contained HTML<br />report generated from KPI<br />snapshots (level gates, error<br />breakdown, cost, calibration<br />curve, loop health, run<br />comparison). Shares panel<br />definitions with the Web UI<br />KPI View; used for D5 and<br />offline reading.</div>"]
      style 74 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#343ced,color:#272834
      75["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Training & Calibration Pipeline</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Python, scikit-learn]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Turns closed cases into<br />candidate changes (prompt,<br />few-shot set, lexicon,<br />thresholds, calibration map),<br />replays them on DEV, and<br />submits them to the promotion<br />gate. Has no read access to<br />locked test labels.</div>"]
      style 75 fill:#d8f1f6,stroke:#343ced,color:#272834
      83["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Agent Tool Library & MCP Server</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Python, MCP Python SDK]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Custom deterministic tools<br />with LLM-oriented docstrings.<br />Pipeline tools are called<br />in-process by the Itemization<br />Agent; analyst tools are<br />served read-only over MCP to<br />Claude Code (team) and to the<br />client's future agent, guided<br />by the skill folder.</div>"]
      style 83 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#343ced,color:#272834
      94["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Guardrail Layer</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Python]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Policy checks around the<br />agent: input guard, tool-call<br />guard, output guard, action<br />guard and privacy guard.<br />Always 'full' in dev and<br />prod; the 'none' and<br />single-guard-off profiles<br />exist only in the experiment<br />environment on synthetic<br />data, for the with/without<br />evaluation.</div>"]
      style 94 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#ef601b,color:#272834
